# i18n for new UI

## User-visible strings

- Never hardcode English in Vue templates or toasts. Use `useI18n()` → `t('namespace.semanticKey')`.
- In `.js` / composable `.ts` files: call `useI18n()` inside the exported composable, not at module top level (ESLint `arivuI18n/no-module-scope-use-i18n`).
- Add keys to `client/src/locales/en/{namespace}.json` (lowerCamelCase, max 3 segments).
- Reuse `actions.*`, `states.*`, `validation.*` when the phrase already exists.

## After adding en keys

```bash
cd client
npm run i18n:sync-keys          # copy new keys to all locales (English placeholder)
npm run i18n:translate-locale -- de   # optional MT for one locale
npm run i18n:check                # CI gate before push
```

## Navigation & tabs

- Sidebar items: set `labelKey` via `buildSidebarFromRegistry` / `navigationLabels.js` (`navigation.*`).
- Tab titles: use `titleKey` + `resolveTabTitle`; record tabs use `moduleRoute` (localized module name + record name).

## System & tenant field labels

- System fields: `{module}.sysField*` + `resolveFieldLabel()` / `useFieldLabel(moduleKey)`.
- Common tenant phrases: `common.phraseAnnualRevenue` style via `configurableLabelResolver.js`.
- Pipeline/stage/picklist values: `deals.stage*` / `deals.picklist*` / `resolveStageOrPicklistLabel()`.
- Picklist options in forms: pass through `localizeSelectOptions()` in `DetailsSection`.

## Do not translate

- Record names, emails, notes, user-generated content.
- Raw API error messages when a semantic `errors.*` code exists.

## CI (automatic)

PRs run `npm run i18n:check` (locale parity, catalog lint, composable `useI18n` scope, missing `t()` keys) and phase hardcoded-string gates on enforced paths. New surfaces must extend `find-hardcoded.mjs` phase scope or stay at 0 hardcoded strings.

See `client/docs/I18N_GUIDELINES.md` and `client/docs/I18N_ROLLOUT.md`.
